ONNX Runtime provides a shared C API and C++ wrappers for ONNX model inference.
This EmberBSD profile uses the CPU execution provider and standard operators.
On NetBSD, device discovery checks an openable DRM node and PCI display devices
in one domain. It does not infer a DRM-to-PCI mapping and declines ambiguous
multi-display selection. CPU discovery remains available. The webgpu option
also ships the shared WebGPU plugin
(libonnxruntime_providers_webgpu.so) built against Dawn (Vulkan backend only)
using the ORT 1.31 Dawn pin and its required contrib operators. Training, Python
bindings, telemetry and CUDA/ROCm/OpenVINO/TensorRT are disabled. Upstream Python
generators run only during the build.
